IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `uc-core`
IMPORT `uc3-sch4-interpretation`
IMPORT `uc3-sch4-payments`

-- The Universal Credit Regulations 2013 (S.I. 2013/376), Schedule 4 (housing costs element for renters): paragraphs 17 to 19, calculations that
-- involve more than one accommodation.
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/uksi-2013-376.txt (plain-text rendering, not the official text). Target: the stable build 1.6.98. Layer 1.
--
-- Whether a renter is treated as occupying two accommodations is Schedule 3 (module uc3-sch3-occupation): paragraph 4 (two dwellings housed by a
-- provider of social housing), paragraph 5 (moving home, new home adapted) and paragraph 6 (fear of violence). This module says how the
-- housing costs element is then calculated. The amounts that Part 4 or Part 5 produce for each accommodation are inputs here.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Paragraph 17: two dwellings treated as a single accommodation are calculated as one, with all their relevant payments and their bedrooms
-- taken together, under Part 5 if the rent for both is owed to a provider of social housing, and under Part 4 in any other case.
-- src:2368 | (1) This paragraph applies to any renter where, under paragraph 4 of Schedule 3 (claimant housed in two dwellings by provider of social housing), two dwellings (“accommodation A” and “accommodation B”) occupied by a renter are treated as the single accommodation in respect of which the renter meets the occupation condition.
-- src:2369 | (2) The amount of the renter's housing costs element is to be determined by a single calculation in respect of accommodation A and accommodation B as if they were one, taking account of—
-- src:2370 | (a) all relevant payments in respect of accommodation A and all relevant payments in respect of accommodation B; and
-- src:2371 | (b) the total number of bedrooms in accommodation A and accommodation B taken together.
-- src:2372 | (3) The single calculation is to be made under Part 5 of this Schedule in any case where the renter's liability to make rent payments in respect of accommodation A and accommodation B is to a provider of social housing.
-- src:2373 | (4) In any other case, the single calculation is to be made under Part 4 of this Schedule.
@ref Sch 4 para 17 (src:2368-2373)
DECLARE `Renter treated as occupying a single accommodation` HAS
    `the landlord that rent payments in respect of accommodation A are payable to`              IS A `Landlord that may be a provider of social housing`
    `the landlord that rent payments in respect of accommodation B are payable to`              IS A `Landlord that may be a provider of social housing`
    `number of bedrooms in accommodation A`                                                     IS A NUMBER
    `number of bedrooms in accommodation B`                                                     IS A NUMBER
    `liabilities for payments in respect of accommodation A`                                    IS A LIST OF `Liability for a payment in respect of accommodation`
    `liabilities for payments in respect of accommodation B`                                    IS A LIST OF `Liability for a payment in respect of accommodation`

-- src:2372 | (3) The single calculation is to be made under Part 5 of this Schedule in any case where the renter's liability to make rent payments in respect of accommodation A and accommodation B is to a provider of social housing.
-- src:2373 | (4) In any other case, the single calculation is to be made under Part 4 of this Schedule.
@ref Sch 4 para 17(3) and (4) (src:2372-2373)
GIVEN renter IS A `Renter treated as occupying a single accommodation`
GIVETH A `Part of Schedule 4 under which the housing costs element is calculated`
`Sch 4 para 17(3) and (4) — the Part under which the single calculation is made` renter MEANS
    IF (`Sch 4 para 2 — provider of social housing` (renter's `the landlord that rent payments in respect of accommodation A are payable to`)) AND (`Sch 4 para 2 — provider of social housing` (renter's `the landlord that rent payments in respect of accommodation B are payable to`))
    THEN `Part 5 (social rented sector)`
    ELSE `Part 4 (private rented sector)`

-- src:2371 | (b) the total number of bedrooms in accommodation A and accommodation B taken together.
@ref Sch 4 para 17(2)(b) (src:2371)
GIVEN renter IS A `Renter treated as occupying a single accommodation`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 4 para 17(2)(b) — the total number of bedrooms in accommodation A and accommodation B taken together` renter MEANS
    (renter's `number of bedrooms in accommodation A`) PLUS (renter's `number of bedrooms in accommodation B`)

-- src:2370 | (a) all relevant payments in respect of accommodation A and all relevant payments in respect of accommodation B; and
@ref Sch 4 para 17(2)(a) (src:2370)
GIVEN renter IS A `Renter treated as occupying a single accommodation`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 4 para 17(2)(a) — the monthly amount of all the relevant payments in respect of accommodation A and accommodation B` renter MEANS
    `Sch 4 para 6 — the monthly amount of all the relevant payments taken into account` (append (renter's `liabilities for payments in respect of accommodation A`) (renter's `liabilities for payments in respect of accommodation B`))

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Paragraph 18: the renter meets the occupation condition for both the new and the old accommodation (Schedule 3 paragraph 5). Step 1: the amount for each
-- under Part 4 or 5. Step 2: add them. Step 3: if housing cost contributions were deducted in both, add back those deducted for the new accommodation.
-- src:2375 | (1) Sub-paragraph (2) applies to any renter where, under paragraph 5 of Schedule 3 (moving home: adaptations to new home for disabled person), the renter meets the occupation condition in respect of both the new accommodation and the old accommodation.
@ref Sch 4 para 18(1) (src:2375)
GIVEN `the renter meets the occupation condition in respect of both the new accommodation and the old accommodation under paragraph 5 of Schedule 3` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 18(1) — sub-paragraph (2) applies` `the renter meets the occupation condition in respect of both the new accommodation and the old accommodation under paragraph 5 of Schedule 3` MEANS
    `the renter meets the occupation condition in respect of both the new accommodation and the old accommodation under paragraph 5 of Schedule 3`

-- src:2376 | (2) The amount of the renter's housing costs element under this Schedule is to be calculated as follows.
-- src:2377 | Step 1
-- src:2378 | Calculate an amount in accordance with Part 4 or Part 5 of this Schedule (as the case may be) in respect of both—
-- src:2379 | (a) the new accommodation; and
-- src:2380 | (b) the old accommodation.
-- src:2381 | Step 2
-- src:2382 | Add together the amounts determined in step 1.
-- src:2383 | Step 3
-- src:2384 | If a deduction was made for housing cost contributions in respect of both the new accommodation and the old accommodation, take the amount of the housing costs contributions deducted in respect of the new accommodation and add that to the amount resulting from step 2.
@ref Sch 4 para 18(2) (src:2376-2384)
GIVEN `amount for the new accommodation` IS A NUMBER
      `amount for the old accommodation` IS A NUMBER
      `a deduction was made for housing cost contributions in respect of both the new accommodation and the old accommodation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `housing cost contributions deducted in respect of the new accommodation` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 4 para 18(2) — the amount of the renter's housing costs element` `amount for the new accommodation` `amount for the old accommodation` `a deduction was made for housing cost contributions in respect of both the new accommodation and the old accommodation` `housing cost contributions deducted in respect of the new accommodation` MEANS
    (`amount for the new accommodation` PLUS `amount for the old accommodation`)
    PLUS (IF `a deduction was made for housing cost contributions in respect of both the new accommodation and the old accommodation` THEN `housing cost contributions deducted in respect of the new accommodation` ELSE 0)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Paragraph 19: the renter meets the occupation condition for both the home and the other accommodation (Schedule 3 paragraph 6(2)). Step 3 adds back
-- the contributions deducted for the accommodation that the renter does NOT normally occupy as their home.
-- src:2387 | (1) Sub-paragraph (2) applies to any renter where, under paragraph 6(2) of Schedule 3 (claimant living in other accommodation because of reasonable fear of violence), the renter meets the occupation condition in respect of both the home accommodation and the other accommodation.
@ref Sch 4 para 19(1) (src:2387)
GIVEN `the renter meets the occupation condition in respect of both the home accommodation and the other accommodation under paragraph 6(2) of Schedule 3` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 4 para 19(1) — sub-paragraph (2) applies` `the renter meets the occupation condition in respect of both the home accommodation and the other accommodation under paragraph 6(2) of Schedule 3` MEANS
    `the renter meets the occupation condition in respect of both the home accommodation and the other accommodation under paragraph 6(2) of Schedule 3`

-- src:2397 | (c) determine which accommodation the renter normally occupies as their home; and
@ref Sch 4 para 19(2) step 3(c) (src:2397)
DECLARE `Accommodation the renter normally occupies as their home` IS ONE OF
    `the home accommodation`
    `the other accommodation`

-- src:2388 | (2) The amount of the renter's housing costs element under this Schedule is to be calculated as follows.
-- src:2389 | Step 1
-- src:2390 | Calculate an amount in accordance with Part 4 or Part 5 of this Schedule (as the case may be) in respect of—
-- src:2391 | (a) the home accommodation; and
-- src:2392 | (b) the other accommodation.
-- src:2393 | Step 2
-- src:2394 | Add together the amounts determined in step 1.
-- src:2395 | Step 3
-- src:2396 | If a deduction was made for housing cost contributions in respect of both the home accommodation and the other accommodation—
-- src:2397 | (c) determine which accommodation the renter normally occupies as their home; and
-- src:2398 | (d) take the amount of the housing costs contributions deducted in respect of the accommodation not so occupied and add that to the amount resulting from step 2.
@ref Sch 4 para 19(2) (src:2388-2398)
GIVEN `amount for the home accommodation` IS A NUMBER
      `amount for the other accommodation` IS A NUMBER
      `a deduction was made for housing cost contributions in respect of both the home accommodation and the other accommodation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `housing cost contributions deducted in respect of the home accommodation` IS A NUMBER
      `housing cost contributions deducted in respect of the other accommodation` IS A NUMBER
      normally IS A `Accommodation the renter normally occupies as their home`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 4 para 19(2) — the amount of the renter's housing costs element` `amount for the home accommodation` `amount for the other accommodation` `a deduction was made for housing cost contributions in respect of both the home accommodation and the other accommodation` `housing cost contributions deducted in respect of the home accommodation` `housing cost contributions deducted in respect of the other accommodation` normally MEANS
    (`amount for the home accommodation` PLUS `amount for the other accommodation`)
    PLUS (IF `a deduction was made for housing cost contributions in respect of both the home accommodation and the other accommodation`
          THEN (CONSIDER normally
                WHEN `the home accommodation`  THEN `housing cost contributions deducted in respect of the other accommodation`
                WHEN `the other accommodation` THEN `housing cost contributions deducted in respect of the home accommodation`)
          ELSE 0)
